      "default": false,
      "description": "If set to true, GPG-sign new commits; defaults to false. This setting overrides the original git configuration `commit.gpgSign` and may be overridden by the command line options `--gpg-sign` and `--no-gpg-sign`.",
      "documented": true,
      "fallback": ["commit.gpgSign"],
      "invalid": "fallback",
      "note": "It decides signing in both directions: git-revise re-creates every commit it rewrites, target and descendants alike, whose signed state differs from this setting, so with it false (the default when `commit.gpgSign` is unset too) a run strips existing signatures even from commits it does not otherwise change. With `gpg.format = ssh` it signs with `gpg.ssh.program`; any other format goes through `gpg.program`.",
      "overriddenBy": ["--gpg-sign", "--no-gpg-sign", "-S"],
