      "defaultDescription": "the value of `rerere.enabled`; when that is unset too, true exactly when the repository's `rr-cache` directory exists (`git rev-parse --git-path rr-cache`, which linked worktrees share with the main one).",
      "defaultExpr": "rr_cache.is_dir()",
      "description": "Whether git-revise replays and records conflict resolutions through git's rerere cache. Read once per conflicted file; when false no resolution is replayed or recorded. When a recorded resolution exists, `rerere.autoUpdate` decides whether it is applied without asking (false prompts `Apply recorded resolution? (y/N)`), which differs from what that key means to git itself.",
